## Continued parity mapping (2026-09-25)

- Added NameServer configured/available list APIs, non-empty list replacement with duplicate removal, selected-address tracking, round-robin initial connection choice, invoke using the selected channel, and a client-owned 30-second availability scan when `scan_available_nameserver` is enabled. Empty NameServer updates are ignored per Java; chosen-address recovery and cleanup are not fully equivalent.
- Added one GO_AWAY reconnect/retry for sync and async invoke with original deadline; a second GO_AWAY returns `TransportError::GoAway`; oneway has no response/retry path.
- Added scripted NameServer invoke/list/availability tests. Tests disable scanning where needed to isolate scripted exchanges; background scan timer lacks controlled-time parity coverage.
- Validation after the NameServer lock fix/test isolation: format, Clippy, workspace tests (49 plus docs), check, metadata checker, Maven verify (17 scenarios/two Rust frames), differential self-test and diff check passed.
- Phase 3 remains NOT MET. Remaining areas include exact callback lifecycle/error taxonomy, Java channel idle/event semantics, processor executor lifecycle, pipeline context, TLS property/config/reload, Netty watermarks/allocator/worker group and full overload flows. No live Broker/Docker test; P3-V04 pending Phase 19. Java checkout untouched.

