- Follow-up parity correction: Java socket buffer settings are signed `int`; Rust config validation now rejects values above `i32::MAX` (not just `u32::MAX`). Reran format check, workspace Clippy, workspace tests (67 unit/integration plus docs) and diff check after this correction — PASS.

## Continuation update (2026-09-25T05:40Z)

- Verified Java `closeChannels` interrupts PULL_MESSAGE and LITE_PULL_MESSAGE response futures; added pending request-address tracking so Rust closes only matching channel pull requests with `TransportError::Interrupted`. Added `p3_close_channels_interrupts_pending_pull_requests_only`.
- Added send-write error classification (`TransportError::Send`) and callback `send_request_ok` semantics for connection/send/TLS failure categories. Hardened processor executor rejection against an executor that runs its FnOnce then reports rejection/panics; shared ownership ensures processor work/rejection response is terminal only once.
- Refined NameServer state: actual channel close clears chosen/available state; successful invoke does not re-mark a channel that closed concurrently. Tests hold peer sockets open while asserting post-response availability, then explicitly close to verify cleanup/recovery. A stale generation close does not evict a replacement.
- During verification fixed a held mutex guard in stale-generation close handling that deadlocked a test runtime; explicitly drop chosen-address guard before connection-table locking. Also corrected a test closure's `FnOnce` type.
- Bidirectional source review reconfirmed Java shuffles updated NameServer lists; Rust currently preserves/deduplicates order (difference documented). Java TLS properties/config/reload/test mode/decryption and server-side TLS settings are not mapped; Rust deliberately retains secure chain/hostname validation rather than Java's insecure test defaults. Netty worker group/pooled allocator/event-loop watermark semantics do not have equivalent Tokio APIs.
- Updated compatibility matrix, README and ADR with current NameServer close behavior, TLS security difference and explicit inventory incompleteness. Full Java public API/overload and config/default/type/range/test-ID ledger is still open; Phase 3 acceptance remains NOT MET, no commit/Phase 4 branch. P3-V04 remains PENDING_PHASE_19; no Broker/Docker run.
